 "name": "pen_merge_drag",
 "description": "Polygon pen merge on a drag and on a click (merge on and off), over a slanted quad in the edited mesh. A point within the merge radius of a quad vertex takes its 3-D position and shares its index, on a click and on every drag event (live: mid-drag the point is already on the vertex). On a DRAG with the global vertex snap type enabled the point snaps onto the vertex but makes its own vertex (no link); a click with the same settings links, and a drag with edge-only, grid-only or no-type snapping links. Edge snap on a drag places the point on the edge's 3-D point under the pointer. The next click's plane passes through the previous point (its height follows a linked or snapped point).",
